hrough debt.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. That raises funding costs but doesn't shut the market.\n\n**Equity: mostly closed**\n- Two utility share offerings were cut back in size, so the weakness is sector-wide.\n- Pellham Power plans 2027 capex up 18%. It withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short. It will now cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves.\n\n**Net view**\n- Norvane can probably fund its plan with debt.\n- Pellham probably can't fund its plan without equity. That is an inference, because the documents give no leverage, rating headroom or debt capacity for Pellham.\n- The sources don't say when equity conditions might improve.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, so its deferrals are a downside risk to 2027 grid-equipment demand. Further spread widening would add to that risk.\n\nSources: the utility-capex-2027, utility-credit and pellham-offering documents (refs n5.r1 and n6.r1).","ttft_ms":1437,"type":"result","duration_ms":25616,"uuid":"7b7ac4b6-f8d3-4851-9b1d-041dc29af934","ttft_stream_ms":984,"time_to_request_ms":111,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":4,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":11,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":3,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":19,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":61,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":63,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":188,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":114,"process_rss_mib_result":197,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":199,"process_cpu_ms_turn":524,